    <h2>About NOHS</h2>
    <p class="lede">Negros Occidental High School (NOHS) is a public school in Bacolod City serving around 9,000 learners in Grades 7 to 12.</p>
    <p>Junior and Senior High School share one campus, so students can grow with the same community from their first year to graduation. Learners follow a strong core curriculum in Grades 7 to 10, then choose from the STEM, ABM, HUMSS, GAS and TVL strands in Senior High School.</p>
    <p>Our teachers and staff work together so that every student feels known, challenged and supported. We are led by our principal, <strong>Dr. Cheryl Juson Tondo</strong>, and we invite families to visit, ask questions and see how our community learns and serves together.</p>
