<section class="gray" id="history">
  <div class="wrap">
   <div class="head hist"><h2>Our history</h2><p>NOHS began in 1902 as Instituto Rizal, the first secondary school in the province, and has carried the name of Negros Occidental High School for most of its long story. It is often still called the "Provincial High School."</p></div>
   <ol class="tl">
    <li><b>1902</b><h3>Instituto Rizal opens</h3><p>Classes begin in rented buildings, with Thomasite Ray Howell as first principal.</p></li>
    <li><b>1927</b><h3>A permanent home</h3><p>Construction of the high school building at the present site is funded.</p></li>
